Subject: GBA SIO: honor clock selection and ignore unarmed peers
Series-Step: 10/19 (mgba_dual 1.6-os4)
Origin: hanbang (this project)
요약: SIOCNT 의 클록 · 전송 속도 비트를 먼저 반영한 뒤 전송을 시작하고, 아직 준비 안 한 상대는 건드리지 않음(젤다 · 유희왕 등 통신 메뉴 정확도).

Start transfers after committing the current SIOCNT clock/baud bits. Keep external-clock Normal transfers armed
until a clock arrives, and keep MULTI child busy read-only. A queued start only clocks peers in the same mode (and armed
external receivers in Normal mode). Reset a participating MULTI child's receive registers and avoid counting event
lateness twice when scheduling its completion.

No new serialized fields are introduced. This is a partial correctness fix, not a fix for the KOF EX2 phase-dependent
disconnect (see 0016 for the SD line and start-bit handling).

---
diff --git a/src/gba/sio.c b/src/gba/sio.c
index 22b79675e796..9f725d07add7 100644
--- a/src/gba/sio.c
+++ b/src/gba/sio.c
@@ -163,6 +163,7 @@ void GBASIOWriteSIOCNT(struct GBASIO* sio, uint16_t value) {
 	int id = 0;
 	int connected = 0;
 	bool handled = false;
+	bool start = false;
 	if (sio->driver) {
 		handled = sio->driver->handlesMode(sio->driver, sio->mode);
 		if (handled) {
@@ -197,9 +198,11 @@ void GBASIOWriteSIOCNT(struct GBASIO* sio, uint16_t value) {
 				sio->p->memory.io[GBA_REG(SIOMULTI2)] = 0xFFFF;
 				sio->p->memory.io[GBA_REG(SIOMULTI3)] = 0xFFFF;
 				sio->rcnt = GBASIORegisterRCNTClearSc(sio->rcnt);
-				_startTransfer(sio);
+				start = true;
 			} else {
-				// TODO
+				// In MULTI a child's busy bit is driven by the parent's
+				// clock, not by writes to its own SIOCNT.
+				value = GBASIOMultiplayerClearBusy(value);
 			}
 		}
 		break;
@@ -210,8 +213,11 @@ void GBASIOWriteSIOCNT(struct GBASIO* sio, uint16_t value) {
 		if (GBASIONormalGetSc(value)) {
 			sio->rcnt = GBASIORegisterRCNTFillSc(sio->rcnt);
 		}
-		if (GBASIONormalIsStart(value) && !GBASIONormalIsStart(sio->siocnt)) {
-			_startTransfer(sio);
+		if (GBASIONormalIsStart(value) && !GBASIONormalIsStart(sio->siocnt)
+		    && GBASIONormalGetSc(value)) {
+			// An external-clock start only arms the shifter. Without
+			// an incoming clock it must remain busy, with no SIO IRQ.
+			start = true;
 		}
 		break;
 	default:
@@ -236,6 +242,11 @@ void GBASIOWriteSIOCNT(struct GBASIO* sio, uint16_t value) {
 		}
 	}
 	sio->siocnt = value;
+	if (start) {
+		// The driver and the completion timer must use this write's
+		// baud/clock selection, including a mode-and-start write.
+		_startTransfer(sio);
+	}
 }
 
 uint16_t GBASIOWriteRegister(struct GBASIO* sio, uint32_t address, uint16_t value) {
